Best way to deal with a large dog: throw food.
Tripe is ideal (because it's not useful for much
else), or if you don't have tripe and can't spare
any other food you can throw fruit, making the
dog peaceful for free.

Food won't help so much with the orcs (though
a tame large dog might).  A wand of digging, fire,
or lightning would definitely help with the orcs,
but if the RNG really wants you dead it will send
in elves next, or an invisible monster with some
kind of wand you aren't resistant to yet.

> So, after clearing the level, 4 swarm mobs spawn
> all within a few hundred turns.  Is this RNG madness

Yes, sometimes the RNG just decides to spawn
monsters faster than you can kill them, so you
have no time to heal.  The usual strategy when
this happens (if you have adequate food) is to
flee upstairs if possible, but I've had games
where that strategy resulted in a crowd of
entirely too many monsters on every explored
level including DL1, and me running out of HP
and fainting from hunger.


